# Copy to the API subdomain document root as `.htaccess` AFTER creating the app in
# cPanel → Setup Python App (cPanel usually writes PassengerAppRoot / PassengerPython).
# If those lines are missing, paste the block cPanel generated, then merge CORS below.
#
# Application root must contain passenger_wsgi.py and manage.py (same folder as this file).

PassengerEnabled On
PassengerAppType wsgi
PassengerStartupFile passenger_wsgi.py

# Optional: only if preflight OPTIONS never reaches Django (see cpanel-api-subdomain.htaccess.example).
# <IfModule mod_headers.c>
#   Header always set Access-Control-Allow-Origin "https://shyam-sweets.com"
#   Header always set Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS"
#   Header always set Access-Control-Allow-Headers "Authorization, Content-Type, Accept, X-CSRFToken"
#   Header always set Access-Control-Max-Age "86400"
# </IfModule>
